<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albanian Fascist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Partia Fashiste e Shqipërisë</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Albanian Fascist Party was the ruling party of Albania under Italian occupation, founded in April 1939 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s invasion and modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s National Fascist Party. Membership was required for many state posts, and the party was subordinate to Italian officials in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a>. It was dissolved in 1943, after the fall of Mussolini.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albanian-fascist-party.jpg" alt="Albanian Fascist Party" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vectorized by Kj1595 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Partia_Fashiste_Shqiptare.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
